{"name":"Wheatfield","hex":"#dfd7bd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Wheatfield","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A place in the United States:\nA township in Clinton County, Illinois.\nA township and town therein, in Jasper County, Indiana.\nA township in Ingham County, Michigan.\nA town in Niagara County, New York.\nA township in Perry County, Pennsylvania.\nAn unincorporated community in Shenandoah County, Virginia.","A township in Clinton County, Illinois."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wheatfield"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Wheat Field","blocks":[{"text":"The Wheat Field is a series of oil paintings executed by Vincent van Gogh in Saint-Rémy-de-Provence. All of them depict the view Van Gogh had from the window of his bedroom on the top floor of the asylum: a field enclosed by stone walls just beneath his window and excluded from normal life by the rear wall of the asylum grounds; beyond this enclosure farm land, accompanied by olive groves and vineyards, ran up to the hills at the foot of the mountain range called Les Alpilles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Van_Gogh_-_Enclosed_Wheat_Field_with_Rising_Sun_%28KM_106.596%29.jpg/330px-Van_Gogh_-_Enclosed_Wheat_Field_with_Rising_Sun_%28KM_106.596%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wheat_Field"},{"title":"The Wheat Field (Constable)","blocks":[{"text":"The Wheat Field is an 1816 landscape painting by the British artist John Constable. It depicts a scene in his native Suffolk. The view across a wheat field depicts a cluster of farm workers who are seen harvesting the crop. Today it is in the Clark Art Institute in Massachusetts having been gifted to the collection in 2007."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/John_Constable%2C_The_Wheat_Field.jpg/330px-John_Constable%2C_The_Wheat_Field.jpg?utm_source=en.w